course: dictionary
lesson: 11085
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Western» is one of these words. It can point to a direction, name part of a country, or name a type of film.
explain: «The empire was split into a western half ruled from Rome and an eastern half ruled from Constantinople.» Here western means the side towards the west, because the sentence also has an eastern half. The clue is the word eastern standing next to it.
explain: «it's Saturday morning for Lily and Saturday evening in Perth, the big city of Western Australia.» Here Western has a capital W and is part of a name. It is the name of a state. Always check the capital letter and the words around it, then swap in your meaning and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Many words have more than one meaning, so always read the context.
fact: «Western» can mean in, from or towards the west, as in «a western wind».
fact: «Western» with a capital letter can describe the countries of Europe and North America and their way of life, as in «Western culture».
fact: «A western» is a film or story about cowboys in the American West in the 1800s.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The empire was split into a western half ruled from Rome and an eastern half ruled from Constantinople.» In this sentence, western means | *In the west, a direction | A kind of cold weather | A film about cowboys | A large city in Australia
exercise: Lily says «a western» must be a kind of sandwich. What is a western? | A type of olive | *A film or story about cowboys in the American West | A kind of sandwich with cheese | A large city in Australia
exercise: «Singing styles differ around the world: Chinese folk and opera singing, Ukrainian folk singing and Western pop use the voice in different ways.» What does Western pop describe? | A cowboy song from the 1800s | Music played only in the west of Australia | *Music from the Western countries of Europe and North America | A wind that blows from the sea
test: «...Saturday evening in Perth, the big city of Western Australia.» What is Western Australia? | *A state of Australia | A kind of olive | A wind from the sea | A film about cowboys
test: «A Mediterranean climate has hot, dry summers and mild, wet winters, and it is found ... in California, central Chile, South Africa's Cape and south-western Australia.» What does south-western mean? | Far away over the sea | Very old and worn out | *Between the south and the west | Loud and busy
exam: Which sentence uses western to mean a film? | *My favourite western has horses, a sheriff and a dusty town. | Western Australia is a big state with a lot of sand. | The western wind blew cold across the lake. | Western culture is shared by many countries.
